 CellLabel->"Out[7]= ",ExpressionUUID->"cc28b187-23ea-48ac-97a8-6256d52d00fb"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The consequence is exactly what the theory predicts: the quotient is ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " quasi-isomorphic to the model. It is three-dimensional with zero \
differential \[LongDash] the cohomology of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "668795ca-8139-487d-8ca5-514f72879080"],
 ", not of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cb4d3fc2-04a1-4994-9d6f-431502ff1132"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"78d329b6-de48-4fe9-b851-3579267c57fd"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"quotient", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NondegenerateQuotient", "[", "bad", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"quotient", "[", "\"\<Basis\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"quotient", "[", "\"\<Differential\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"HodgeTypeReport", "[", "bad", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "\"\<Cohomology\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"13566efa-728f-4fbe-90c8-3df3c76d815e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "a", ",", 
     SuperscriptBox["a", "2"]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "2"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[8]= ",ExpressionUUID->"9fb51b56-265d-4b21-ba31-94ac456fa892"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three against two: the quotient map has killed the class of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c5f5415-67d3-4c8b-bf00-4515dac5204f"],
 " but not the class ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df556ff6-93be-4d6e-84ef-9ac37a790849"],
 " that ought to have died with it. The repair in the reference is to ",
 StyleBox["extend", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58cefba6-da75-4499-af49-58d77cc3fa6c"],
 " to a larger PDGA of Hodge type that retracts onto it; the extension \
adjoins a generator in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8134dea-6abe-4a1e-b8c3-de9ed638ba58"],
 ", which is why this example also shows that no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b390882-54fc-4baf-8308-523d1004268c"],
 "-connected extension of Hodge type exists in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2918fe56-9ac1-4fb9-8b62-d7d27a3689d4"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f4be940-2493-431b-8cdb-6da79781aa6b"],

Cell["When the model is already a dPD algebra", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e1784b13-d091-46c1-8fcc-8c1196c73aa2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At the other extreme are models whose pairing is already perfect on chain \
level, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["deg",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a10423b-ea59-4b08-b9b1-ad8112859bc2"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03242b64-051a-40e9-b761-062eeec99d46"],
 ". The minimal model of a nilmanifold is one: a finite-dimensional exterior \
algebra on generators of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c082759-abef-44c8-9c19-0eb158aac3e0"],
 ", with the differential of the nilpotent Lie algebra."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd9f332b-d138-4f4b-b0ab-375a925beb17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The three-dimensional Heisenberg nilmanifold has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8fd83092-3bc4-4a2b-957f-2c022c77aed0"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "760d8d21-265b-4f69-b211-d864863b69ec"],
 ", and the volume form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"x", "y", "z"}], "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50738eca-0be0-42a7-aa69-8215f75e6739"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e70895a2-ab1e-46d2-8caf-ae9c7e3bbcef"],

